WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.

8
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.220
Birthday, everybody.

9
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.640
It is Michael's birthday.

10
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.640
Michael, it's your B-Day.

11
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.120
Oh, my gosh.

12
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.260
Oh, Angela, he would be so happy if anyone responded to his birthday like that.

13
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.380
Yeah, this guy needs a party like nobody else.

14
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.860
He needs the party.

15
00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:42.500
It's so true.

16
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:51.120
Guys, it's season two, episode 19, Michael's birthday, written by Lee Eisenberg and Gene Stepnitsky, directed by Ken Whittingham.

17
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.480
Guys, I'm in my closet right now.

18
00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.260
I am in my That's What She Should.

19
00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:00.600
This morning, my husband figured out how to try to soundproof it, Sam.

20
00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.800
I don't know if we did it.

21
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:02.300
We tried.

22
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:10.280
We got a shower curtain out of the guest room, and Josh put it across the shed and hung some blankets on it.

23
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.500
We took, you know the clamps that our kids have a fort building kit?

24
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:14.920
Wow.

25
00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.580
And we took all of their clamps.

26
00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:21.820
So I hope the kids don't get to do a fort this week because mom is trying to podcast from home.

27
00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:31.420
The best part of seeing you right now on this video chat while we do this is that you are wearing a set of gamer headphones.

28
00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:32.700
Yes, I am.

29
00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.400
I have a giant microphone, but I've pointed it up to the sky.

30
00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.080
Like an antenna coming out of your ear.

31
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.260
Yeah, that's true.

32
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.020
And we're going to put a photo of this on the pod.

33
00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.360
Should I do a summary?

34
00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:45.440
Here it is.

35
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.480
Do a summary, babe.

36
00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.720
I don't know why I called you babe.

37
00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:49.460
I don't know.

38
00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.620
I don't know either.

39
00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.500
Do a summary, babe.

40
00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:58.280
It's Michael's birthday, and he is desperate to be the center of attention.

41
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:05.740
Meanwhile, we learn that Kevin is waiting for the results of a mole biopsy.

42
00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:06.140
Yes.

43
00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:07.360
Kevin is very worried.

44
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:14.500
He might have skin cancer, and this is causing a distraction to Michael's birthday that he is unhappy with.

45
00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:15.160
Oh, my gosh.

46
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:19.200
Michael's like, today is the day for celebration, and you guys are all worried about Kevin.

47
00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.060
And I am grumpy about it.

48
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:21.420
Yeah.

49
00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.600
There's my summary.

50
00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:24.780
I like it, babe.

51
00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:26.160
Babe, I like it.

52
00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:27.900
Babe.

53
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:28.920
Okay, wait.

54
00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.220
Are we just going to jump right in?

55
00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.060
Should we jump right in?

56
00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.160
No, there's more summary.

57
00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:33.940
And fast facts.

58
00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.580
You've forgotten everything.

59
00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:36.460
Wow.

60
00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:37.420
There's more summary.

61
00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:38.600
What is happening?

62
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:46.880
Also, in this episode, Dwight and Angela really bicker over who exactly is in charge of planning Michael's birthday party.

63
00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:53.120
Is it Dwight as his right-hand man, or is it Angela, head of the PPC?

64
00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:58.080
This is the first time we're going to see a little tension going on between Dwight and Angela.

65
00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.000
Yeah.

66
00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:04.880
Well, I mean, there was tension in season one over who was the security officer, you know.

67
00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.800
That was pre-them dating.

68
00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.480
So they have some issues about who gets to have control of what.

69
00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.760
They had that going into this relationship.

70
00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:19.120
And I have a note card, guys, that says, Dwight and Angela sass.

71
00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.400
Ooh, Dwight and Angela sass.

72
00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:22.700
All through this episode.

73
00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:23.820
We're going to track it.

74
00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:28.500
Also in this episode, Jim and Pam, they sneak out of the office together.

75
00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:34.020
And in the end, the entire office gang is going to go ice skating.

76
00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.340
Who saw that coming?

77
00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:36.560
I didn't see that coming.

78
00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.340
Well, the writers knew that we were going to end up at an ice skating rink.

79
00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:45.460
That leads me into, Sam, please play my special audio clip.

80
00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.460
Fast fact!

81
00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.210
Submit some little, they're called stings, Angela.

82
00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:56.410
I love that so much.

83
00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:58.050
I didn't even know there was such a thing.

84
00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:58.470
Yeah.

85
00:03:58.970 --> 00:03:59.550
Thank you.

86
00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.730
So more stings, please.

87
00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.510
More stings, guys.

88
00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:04.670
Send us your stings.

89
00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.570
I didn't even know that was a term.

90
00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:07.970
We're learning so much.

91
00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.630
We're a hundred, but thank you for making us stings.

92
00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:17.710
So fast fact number one is that Steve Carell is a very, very good ice skater.

93
00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:21.010
He played hockey growing up.

94
00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:24.310
He played pickup hockey every week as an adult.

95
00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:31.510
Fan question from Matt Loveless, was the plot built around Steve's ability to ice skate?

96
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.470
Yes.

97
00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:33.710
He's so good.

98
00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:34.890
He's really good.

99
00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:41.290
Yes, the writers had on one of their cards up on the wall this fact about Steve being

100
00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:45.530
a good ice skater, and they had been looking forever for a way to incorporate it.

101
00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:54.630
And you guys might remember that later when we filmed the Threat Level Midnight, that again,

102
00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:59.310
that plot of Threat Level Midnight, the movie, takes place in an ice skating rink.

103
00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:04.150
And that was just like another opportunity to feature Steve's ice skating ability.

104
00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:08.430
I was at the car wash one time waiting for my car to get washed, right?

105
00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:12.250
You know, the one you kind of, you can drive through part of it, and then you wait on the

106
00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.170
other side, right?

107
00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:13.590
Yeah.

108
00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:17.950
So I'm at the car wash, and this guy walks up to me and goes, I ice skate with Steve.

109
00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.650
Just, you know, sometimes I ice skate with Steve.

110
00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:22.210
And I was like, oh, what?

111
00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:22.910
Oh, okay.

112
00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.710
Well, way to go.

113
00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:28.230
You're probably very good because Steve is good.

114
00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:29.170
Have a nice day.

115
00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:34.790
Well, you know, Angela, my husband Lee ice skates, he's on several pickup hockey teams,

116
00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.310
and my son as well is a hockey player.

117
00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:43.510
And my husband now plays on the pickup team that Steve used to play on.

118
00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:47.210
I wonder if he plays with the guy from the car wash.

119
00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:50.330
Steve does not play pickup hockey anymore, he told me.

120
00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.010
He kind of retired from that.

121
00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.910
But back when we shot this episode, he was really into it.

122
00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:56.410
He was really into it.

123
00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:58.150
And Jenna, you're like a hockey mom.

124
00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:03.090
I have been on the ice with you now, and I've met your hockey mom friends, and I am into

125
00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:03.370
it.

126
00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:08.430
I don't have a kid that plays hockey, but they told me you can drink beer at like 10 a.m.

127
00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:09.210
hockey matches.

128
00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:12.330
And I'm like, I think this is the crowd I should be in.

129
00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.130
I mean, I'm over at the soccer field.

130
00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.590
They got nothing at that concession stand.

131
00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.070
Maybe some pretzels.

132
00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:22.770
I mean, we're at these hockey rinks sometimes at 7 in the morning or 8 in the morning, and

133
00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:26.710
they open up that concession stand, and they go for it.

134
00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:33.830
I am not a beer drinker, but I am amazed at people's ability to have a glass of beer in

135
00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:34.190
the morning.

136
00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:35.990
I'm like, that would do me in.

137
00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:38.910
But yeah, oh God, I love the hockey community.

138
00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:41.270
It's a great, great community.

139
00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:43.950
I love being a part of it.

140
00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:44.250
All right.

141
00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:45.530
Fast fact number two.

142
00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:48.490
This is a fan question from Renata.

143
00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:52.750
She said, this episode has several external locations.

144
00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:56.870
Did it take longer to produce this episode because of that?

145
00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:02.890
So we usually would take five days to shoot an episode, and we were still able to shoot

146
00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.770
this episode in five days, even with our multiple locations.

147
00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:07.630
And guess what I did, Angela?

148
00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:08.190
What?

149
00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:13.110
I got some scoop from Kentopedia about our locations.

150
00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:14.430
Kent Sabornak.

151
00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:15.150
Let's hear it.

152
00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:16.210
All right.

153
00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:22.490
So first up, the store that Jim and Pam go to was a Rite Aid at Woodman and Sherman

154
00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:22.770
Way.

155
00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.130
Do you remember that Rite Aid, Angela?

156
00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:25.050
I do.

157
00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:26.430
I do.

158
00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:30.170
I pass by it every day on the way to work, and I would shop there constantly.

159
00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:30.770
Yeah.

160
00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:34.110
I would always pick up some milk on the way home.

161
00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:36.210
One time I bought some socks.

162
00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:37.630
I was low on socks.

163
00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:40.450
Oh, I remember setting up my trailer.

164
00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:44.210
We would sort of decorate, and I got a few different little things.

165
00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:47.730
I got like a doormat at that Rite Aid.

166
00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:48.630
Okay, so cute.

167
00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:50.010
You were at the Rite Aid by us.

168
00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:54.230
He said that we shot there for a half a day, but we started very, very early.

169
00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.790
I think my hair and makeup started around 4 a.m.

170
00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:57.930
or 4.30 a.m.

171
00:07:57.970 --> 00:07:58.610
I believe it.

172
00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:05.750
Because, yeah, we had to start shooting on camera by 6, and the Rite Aid said we could

173
00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:09.050
only shoot there until 11 a.m.

174
00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:10.870
with the store closed.

175
00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:15.190
After 11 a.m., we could keep shooting, but they were going to let customers in.

176
00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:18.550
And Kent said that we finished by 10 a.m.

177
00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:24.230
We finished an hour early, and that all the customers that you see in those scenes are hired

178
00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:25.230
background performers.

179
00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:26.630
None of them are real customers.

180
00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:28.010
All right?

181
00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:29.050
Good job, team.

182
00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:29.630
Good job.

183
00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:31.510
You got in.

184
00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:32.290
You got out.

185
00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:33.650
That's the scoop on the Rite Aid.

186
00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:38.650
So the ice skating, we shot that at Pickwick Ice Rink in Burbank.

187
00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:40.530
I know this rink well.

188
00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:44.430
And we had the whole place to ourselves for one full day.

189
00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.870
We were there from 7 a.m.

190
00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:46.890
to 7 p.m.

191
00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:51.330
Again, we started our hair and makeup very early, around 5 a.m., and we were all shooting

192
00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:51.930
by 7.

193
00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:56.630
The other skaters in the background were background actors.

194
00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:58.370
We shut that place down.

195
00:08:58.630 --> 00:08:59.490
It was all ours.

196
00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:07.530
So Kent also told me that luckily, both Randall Einhorn and Matt Soane, they were our camera

197
00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:09.970
operators, that they could ice skate.

198
00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:12.810
And so they were skating around with cameras.

199
00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:14.510
Do you remember that, Angela?

200
00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:18.050
Because I did not remember that those guys were skating with us.

201
00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.070
I remember Randall on the ice.

202
00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:20.690
I do.

203
00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:26.050
Because I have a little funny backstory about there was a stunt ice skater, Jenna.

204
00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:27.730
Do you remember the stunt ice skater?

205
00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:28.410
Oh, yeah.

206
00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:30.510
The guy who filled in for Oscar.

207
00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:31.230
Yes.

208
00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:36.410
So you'll see later in the episode as we watch it that Oscar is like a very good ice skater.

209
00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:39.850
He does like a kind of a pirouette and spins around.

210
00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:44.390
Well, that's because there was a stunt guy that looked like him that was a really great

211
00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.290
figure skater.

212
00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:47.770
And I have a little story about that.

213
00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:52.650
I don't know if you remember this, Jenna, but Randall was filming the stunt guy getting

214
00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:53.890
all of the moves, right?

215
00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:54.670
Yeah.

216
00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:57.310
And they wanted us skating in the background.

217
00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:58.770
And I sort of skated in the background.

218
00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:00.890
And I did a big circle.

219
00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:02.990
Like, I kind of opened my legs and did a big circle.

220
00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:07.710
And the guy said to me in between takes, he goes, hey, he said, can you skate?

221
00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:09.250
And I was like, well, I can roller skate.

222
00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.770
So I'm just trying to do what I do on roller skates.

223
00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:12.710
And he said, come here.

224
00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:14.390
And he spun me around.

225
00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:17.510
And then Randall was like, oh, wait, I'll get this.

226
00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:22.330
Just in case, maybe it'll be funny that Oscar spins Angela or something, you know?

227
00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:22.670
Okay.

228
00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:27.150
And so the stunt ice skater started doing all these things with me, Jenna.

229
00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:27.930
He spun me.

230
00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:29.590
He picked me up and twirled me.

231
00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:32.630
He had me stick one leg out and one leg up.

232
00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:35.610
Like, and then spun me and set me down.

233
00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:41.390
And we, like somewhere there is footage of the stunt ice skater lifting me in the air

234
00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:42.790
and spinning me around.

235
00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:44.610
Where is this footage?

236
00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:51.030
We never used the footage, but it really made me laugh to think that maybe there is a world

237
00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:54.250
where Angela and Oscar figure skate together.

238
00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:55.690
Okay.

239
00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:56.770
Two things.

240
00:10:56.970 --> 00:11:00.930
Number one, NBC released this footage immediately.

241
00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:04.290
Number two, Angela, do you know who that guy was?

242
00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:05.670
I looked him up.

243
00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:09.190
Okay, his name is Bert Jude Lankin.

244
00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:09.650
Okay.

245
00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:18.670
And he was a pair skater, a famous pair skater who won the silver medal at the 1982 United States

246
00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:25.470
Figure Skating Championships and then later placed sixth at the 1984 Winter Olympic Games.

247
00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:26.610
Wow!

248
00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:32.030
You were figure skating with an Olympic pairs figure skater.

249
00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:33.530
Where is this footage?

250
00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:34.990
That is amazing.

251
00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:36.270
That is so cool.

252
00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.970
